{
  "$comment": "#EXP-1699 (owner 2026-11-05: 'Add PRs ready to merge'): `pullRequests` in the input adds PR ROWS to the same fold (`prCases`, every mirror compares the WHOLE array): a PR is a row while `state` is `open`, `checksState` is `success`, its root session is synced (an ended chat's PR still waits; another member's agent conversation never), no session of that root is `busy` (working = not yet on a person, chat-list `chatRowWord`), and `basePullRequestId` is null or names a PR that is neither `open` nor `draft` (a stacked PR waits on its base, not on a person). A draft PR is the synced `state: draft`, so it is never a row, and a PR stacked on a draft waits too. A PR ROW: messageId = the PR's id, sessionId = rootId = the root, kind `pr`, opens `results` (the chat's Results tab, which holds the PR block; an agent conversation has no such tab: `chat`), title = the PR's title, chat = the root's name, meta = `#<number>`, age and createdAt from the PR's createdAt; PR rows sit UNDER every plan and question (owner on #EXP-1699: 'Keep plans and questions on top'), each group newest first; the entry's count includes them. Glyph `pr-open`. #FEED-191 (owner 2026-11-04: 'decisions (plan/questions) = new ... new menu entry when there are decisions (hidden otherwise, similar to drafts): Needs you ... opens in detail page view of the chat! but on the correct tab'). NEEDS YOU ×4: every waiting plan and question the viewer can act on. FOLD `needsYou({now, me, sessions, messages})` (every mirror replays `cases`, comparing the WHOLE array): `sessions` = the viewer's synced sessions {id, rootId, name (session-title; an agent conversation = the agent's name), status, agentId, userId}, minus `ended` ones and another member's agent conversation; `messages` = the conversations' DIGESTS (chats.json `digestMessages`; never a transcript: EXP-1380; #FEED-191 (owner 2026-11-05): a digest carries EVERY waiting card of its conversation (`waits`), so the list is FLAT: three decisions waiting in one chat = three rows, each opening its own plan or question, never one row per chat), a repeated id once. A ROW per waiting card: a `plan` / `question` with `answeredAt` null (a digest's card is cut: it keeps no `decision`, so the timestamp is what settles it) whose waiting-cards.json `cardState` is `waiting`; an `ask` mirror with `answeredAt` null names its ORIGIN (a digest keeps the ask card's `sessionId` + `messageId`, chats.ts `digestMessage` and the SQL `conversation_digest_message`): when the viewer may read the origin session (ended included), its copy is not `private.*` and the card names a `messageId`, the row carries the origin's ids (the origin's own card, when it is also in the digests, wins: one row). An older digest without `messageId`: the row opens the origin's chat (`card`), dropped when that origin session already has its own row. An unreadable origin or a neutral body: the mirror's own ids and session, with the neutral copy (chats.json `askPreview`). A row: messageId, sessionId, rootId, kind, opens (`plan` = a plan the viewer can read and whose message is named: the chat's Plan tab on THAT plan; `card` = a question, or a private mirror: the chat's Conversation scrolled to the card, THE waiting chip's `selectWaiting`), title (a plan = plan-page `planRowLabel`; a question = ask-dock `askDockTitle`, blank = `askDockLabel`; a mirror = `askPreview`'s text less `prefix.question`), chat (the ROOT's name), meta (``; a PR's `#<number>`; a digest's plan is cut and pictureless, so no counts), age (results-tab.json `resultAge`), createdAt. Order: NEWEST first (createdAt desc, then messageId desc). THE ENTRY (`copy.entry`, the concept `nav-needs-you`, a count Badge = the rows' length; none = NO entry; as Drafts): WIDE (web md+, the IDE) = a sidebar root entry right after Agent, the nav order Agent · Needs you · Chats · Devices · Drafts; PHONES (iOS, Android, web-mobile) = the FIRST row of the Chats list above the Agents section, as tall as the Archived row (chats.json): the glyph in the needs-you tone centred in the `leadDisc`-wide column, no disc, title `copy.entry`, the count Badge in the needs-you tone trailing, testId `testIds.entry`; a press pushes THE list. THE LIST (`route`; phones: pushed, the page header `copy.entry` with the back control; wide: the content card, no header) = one reading column of THE inbox page's ListRow (`list` density): the leading glyph in the needs-you tone (waiting-cards.json `icons`: plan `coding-plan`, question `ui-help`), line 1 the title (medium, truncated) then `age` muted trailing, line 2 `chat` then ` · meta` (when set), muted, truncated; testId `testIds.row`. No row = THE EmptyState (`copy.empty`, no subtitle; the route stays reachable, e.g. after the last answer). A press opens the chat by `opens`: the chat screen (`sessionId`'s own target, inbox-route.json `sessionTarget`) WITH its normal header and strip on the right tab; a `plan` = plan-page.json `route`'s redirect. AFTER A DECISION: plan-page.json (any decision on the Plan tab returns to the Conversation). Mirrors: desktop domain::needs_you, iOS ExpCore NeedsYou.swift, Android domain/NeedsYou.kt. Styleguide `needs-you` (Exponential-specific, not eUI) draws `cases[1]`'s rows and the phone entry row. #EXP-1707 (merge-train.json NEEDS YOU): with the merge train the EXP-1699 PR rows hold only in `approval` mode (their tap = Needs approval); in `auto` mode (the default) no PR waits for a person, and a STUCK PR (merge-train `stuckRow`: held after 3 bounces or 24 h, or a fix waiting 2 h+ on an offline device) is the one PR row, titled `Auto-merge stuck on #N` with Retry, Merge now (owners) and Close PR; every `prCases` input carries `mergeMode` (the ready rows = `approval`; the `auto` case lists none). #EXP-1710: an `approval` ready row's PRESS is Needs approval, never the chat: THE pill's confirm (prompts.json merge-issue-pr / merge-run-pr, or the stack confirm when the PR has an open stack beneath it), Merge queues it, Cancel leaves the row; a stuck row's press opens `results`, its buttons act. Styleguide `needs-you` adds ONE stuck row (merge-train `stuckRow` cases[0]: `Auto-merge stuck on #12`, `3 bounces`, Retry · Merge now · Close PR) under `cases[1]`'s rows ×4, the desktop twin included. The stuck rows replay in merge-train.json `stuckRow` (web and desktop fold them beside `needsYou()`, iOS and Android inside it).",
